BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Food Justice Undone: Book Talk with Author Hanna Garth
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T190000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52693977784372
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a talk with Dr. Hanna Garth\, assistant pro
 fessor of anthropology at Princeton University and author of the new book\
 , Food Justice Undone: Lessons for Building a Better Movement. Garth be jo
 ined by Charlotte Biltekof\, Darrell Corti Endowed Professor in Food\, Win
 e\, and Culture at UC Davis.\n\nFood Justice Undone explores the stakes of
  social justiceand the possibility of multiracial coalitions working towar
 d a better future. Drawing on 12 years of ethnographic research\, Garth’
 s book examines what motivates people from affluent\, majority-white areas
  of the city to intervene in South Central LA. Garth argues that "food jus
 tice" and "healthy food" operate as racially coded language\, reinforcing 
 the idea that health problems in low-income Black & Brown communities can 
 be solved through individual behavior rather than structural change.\n\nGa
 rth’s research focuses on the systems and processes that impede access t
 o basic needs for marginalized people. She has specifically analyzed probl
 ems with food access and the inequities of the global industrial food syst
 em\, as well as the ways people struggle to overcome structural inequaliti
 es and prejudice in their attempts to access basic needs. Garth is also th
 e author of Food in Cuba: The Pursuit of a Decent Meal and the coeditor of
  Black Food Matters: Racial Justice in the Wake of Food Justice.\n\nThis e
 vent is open to all.
LOCATION:Shields Library\, 167
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/food-justice-undone-book-talk
 -with-author-hanna-garth
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
